---

<section class="section actone" id="problem" aria-labelledby="actone-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="actone__grid">
      <div class="actone__lead reveal">
        <h2 class="actone__title" id="actone-title">
          Your building wastes about a third of the energy it buys. So why
          didn't your last upgrade pay off?
        </h2>
        <p class="actone__stat ph" data-countup="30" data-prefix="~" tabindex="0">~30%</p>
        <p class="actone__stat-note">
          That's the EPA's figure for the average commercial building. Most
          hotels have never had anyone qualified find out where theirs goes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="actone__body reveal">
        <p class="actone__hook">
          Here's the irony: the upgrades you bought to cut your energy use may
          be quietly fighting each other.
        </p>
        <ul class="actone__chain">
          <li>
            <span class="actone__cause">Each vendor optimized the one thing they sell</span>
            <span class="actone__arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            <span class="actone__effect">then left.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="actone__cause">The pieces were never designed to work together</span>
            <span class="actone__arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            <span class="actone__effect">so they interfere.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="actone__cause">Power quality degrades</span>
            <span class="actone__arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            <span class="actone__effect">equipment runs harder and fails years sooner.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="actone__cause">The savings on the brochure</span>
            <span class="actone__arr" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            <span class="actone__effect">quietly leak away.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="actone__turn">
          That isn't bad luck. Every vendor gets paid to install their box, so
          none of them owns the result. Your building wasn't left incoherent by
          accident. It was left incoherent by incentive. The operators who stop
          overpaying have one thing in common: they measured before they bought.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .actone {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .actone__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 360px), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .actone__title {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    max-width: 20ch;
  }
  .actone__hook {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink) !important;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .actone__stat {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6rem);
    line-height: 0.9;
    color: var(--gold-text);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }
  .actone__stat-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--body);
    max-width: 44ch;
  }
  .actone__body {
    padding-top: var(--space-2xs);
  }
  .actone__body p {
    color: var(--body);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .actone__chain {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-l) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .actone__chain li {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-s);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .actone__chain li:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
  .actone__cause { color: var(--ink); }
  .actone__arr {
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: #e0894a;
  }
  .actone__effect { color: var(--muted); }
  .actone__turn {
    margin-top: var(--space-l);
    color: var(--ink) !important;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .actone__body.reveal {
      transition-delay: 0.1s;
    }
  }
</style>
